Day 5 takeaway (Part 1/2) -

Simple CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)
name: CI/CD Pipeline

on:
  push:
    branches: [ "main" ]   # Run pipeline when code is pushed to main branch
  pull_request:
    branches: [ "main" ]

jobs:
  build-and-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    
    steps:
      # Step 1: Checkout source code
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      # Step 2: Set up Node.js (example project)
      - name: Set up Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '18'

      # Step 3: Install dependencies
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm install

      # Step 4: Run tests
      - name: Run tests
        run: npm test

  deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    needs: build-and-test   # Run only if build-and-test passes
    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'   # Only deploy from main branch
    
    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v3

      # Example deploy (here we just simulate deployment)
      - name: Deploy to server
        run: echo "🚀 Deploying application..."

🔎 What this pipeline does:
Trigger: Runs when you push to main or create a PR.

Build & Test Job:

Checks out the code.

Installs dependencies.

Runs automated tests.

Deploy Job:

Runs only if tests pass.

(Here it just prints “Deploying…” but in real life you’d deploy to AWS, GCP, Azure, or a server).

It is a very basic pipeline. Please let me know how it can be better.
